OL,3,GNEWSAWork to preserve dead 'Robin Hood'
OL,4,Aoak tree begins
OL,5,
OL,6,FWork to preserve one of the UK's most
OL,7,Ficonic oak trees has begun, three
OL,8,Fmonths after experts confirmed it had
OL,9,Fdied.
OL,11,FThe Major Oak is estimated to have
OL,12,Flived in Sherwood Forest in
OL,13,FNottinghamshire for up to 1,200 years,
OL,14,Fand has links to the legend of Robin
OL,15,FHood.
OL,17,FThe Royal Society for the Protection of
OL,18,FBirds (RSPB) - the conservation charity
OL,19,Fwhich manages the forest - said in
OL,20,FJune, after the tree's first spring
OL,21,Fwith no leaves, the Major Oak had died.
OL,23,APub: 30-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,369,360,200,160,0,100
